From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:45:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Get all keys, values and records with
 IDBGetAllOptions

getAll() and getAllKeys() of object stores and indexes take an
IDBGetAllOptions dictionary ({query, count, direction}) in place of the
query, and the new getAllRecords() gives IDBRecord objects (key,
primaryKey, value) for the same reads, as the IndexedDB editor's draft
has them ("create a request to retrieve multiple items").

Protocol: GetAllKeys and GetAllItems carry a direction. GetAllRecords
replies RequestOutput::AllRecords, a list of IndexedDBRecord snapshots:
the index key (the primary key for a store), the primary key and the
value. It is its own output variant, so that a record list can't be
taken for Iterate's cursor step.

Backend: queries::retrieve_multiple_items reads all three kinds with one
statement on P3.3's RecordSource path, ORDER BY DESC for "prev" and
"prevunique", and for the unique directions of a non-unique index with
P3.4's NOT EXISTS condition, which keeps the record with the lowest
primary key of each key (RDB can't read MIN/MAX of BLOBs). "prevunique"
gives the last count keys in descending order, as a cursor visits them
and WPT expects; the spec's loop text would keep the first count keys.

Script: IDBRequest::retrieve_multiple_items takes QueryOrOptions. A
first argument that is a potentially valid key range is a query; so are
undefined and null, so that getAll(null, count) keeps its count, as WPT
expects. Anything else converts to IDBGetAllOptions, whose count
replaces the count argument. "is a potentially valid key range" checks
the types that convert_value_to_key converts, so array getters run once.
IDBRecord (new interface, Window and Worker) converts its keys on first
access and keeps the converted values; the values of records go through
IDBObjectStore::deserialize_value, so generated keys are injected.

Tests: backend test_get_all_retrieves_what_a_cursor_visits (store and
non-unique, unique and multiEntry indexes, every direction, range and
count, against a reference filter and P3.4's spec cursor reference), fork
WPT get-all-options.any.js (directions and counts on indexes whose keys
have several records, records with generated keys, query vs. options and
the exception order, IDBRecord's attributes), IDBRecord in the interface
lists. Expectations updated for the tests that pass now.

Validation: `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits` (host SQLite): 141 passed, 1 skipped (P3 tip 140/1); the new test fails with the unique-direction condition removed. Host WPT tests/wpt/tests/IndexedDB (4,511 subtests), 8 processes: SpiderMonkey 4,465, QuickJS 4,463 (P3 tip 3,970 / 3,970); the same 495 new passes on both engines, in idbobjectstore_getAll-options (69), _getAllKeys-options (60), _getAllRecords (75), idbindex_getAll-options (87), _getAllKeys-options (84), _getAllRecords (87) and idlharness's getAllRecords and IDBRecord subtests (33), no other subtest changed but known flips (SM idbfactory-origin-isolation TIMEOUT, QuickJS idbcursor-continuePrimaryKey-exception-order.any.sharedworker TIMEOUT after its worker variant, 5 of 5 OK alone); expectations updated with `./mach update-wpt` from both engines' runs filtered to those 7 tests. /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ with the new get-all-options.any.js (5 subtests in 3 globals) and the interface lists: 204 of 204 on SM, QuickJS as expected (interfaces FAIL there as before). DAYU200 (QuickJS + RDB, 2 processes): WPT IndexedDB/ 4,446 (P3 tip 3,953), the host's new passes, other changes only the known flips (idb-partitioned-coverage timing out as a whole, the lone-surrogate subtest of idbobjectstore-rename-store.any.sharedworker), /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ 202 of 202; a 50,000-record probe there: getAllRecords 5.2 s on a store and 8.1 s on an index (getAll 3.9 s, getAllKeys 0.9 s), reads of another connection meanwhile 2 to 20 ms, servoshell RSS peak 260 MiB against 248 MiB while the records were put; `./mach test-unit --ohos -p servo-storage` RDB only 142 passed / 3 skipped, SQLite and RDB 253 / 4. `./mach check --ohos -- -p servo-storage --all-targets` with SQLite, RDB and both: no warnings; `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings` and `RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings" ./mach build --use-crown --locked --profile checked-release` pass; `./mach fmt`; test-tidy passes but the known libsqlite3-sys advisory.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implemented the getAll options, getAllRecords and IDBRecord in script and backend, wrote the unit and fork WPT tests, ran the host and board checks and the board probe, updated the expectations)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
